<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
    HSK patch: gate VFE Mechanoids raids by replacing the
    raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve on VFE_Mechanoid so they don't
    appear in early-game / low-wealth / tribal scenarios.

    Why?
    Like the Junker pirates issue, low-tier VFE mechs (basic
    Lancer/Scyther variants) have low enough combatPower that the
    storyteller can squeeze them into a 200-400 point early raid
    budget. Result: tribal stone-age colonies getting hit by mech
    raids on day 4.

    Note: previous attempt used <minTotalPoints> on each
    pawnGroupMaker. That field doesn't exist on PawnGroupMakerMech
    — RimWorld silently ignored it (XML errors in log) and the patch
    was a no-op. The correct mechanism is raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve
    on the FactionDef itself: when commonality reaches 0, the
    storyteller can't pick the faction for a raid.

    Mechs are intended as a late-game threat (need charge tech / EMP
    to fight back), so the threshold is higher than the 800 used for
    Junker pirates — 1500 raid points (~80k+ wealth, charge tech
    researched, plasteel armor available).

    VFE Mechanoid's default curve is:
        (300,  0)
        (700,  1)
        (1400, 2)
        (2800, 2.5)
        (4000, 2.8)

    Replacement curve gates at 1500:
        (0, 0)         — no raids at any low budget
        (1499, 0)      — still 0 right up to the threshold
        (1500, 0.001)  — barely above 0 at the threshold (sharp step)
        (2800, 2.5)    — VFE's normal late-game weight
        (4000, 2.8)    — VFE's normal end-game weight

    The (1499, 0) → (1500, 0.001) step is intentional — it produces an
    effectively step-function gate while keeping the curve interpolated.
-->
<Patch>

    <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
        <xpath>Defs/FactionDef[defName="VFE_Mechanoid"]/raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve</xpath>
        <value>
            <raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve>
                <points>
                    <li>(0, 0)</li>
                    <li>(1499, 0)</li>
                    <li>(1500, 0.001)</li>
                    <li>(2800, 2.5)</li>
                    <li>(4000, 2.8)</li>
                </points>
            </raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve>
        </value>
    </Operation>

</Patch>
